Rule 1 (probability values in p must be strictly between 0 and 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (min(v_1) > 0 ∧ max(v_1) < 1)
>>
Rule 2 (scale parameter must be strictly positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (p, loc, and scale must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3)
>>
Rule 4 (p and loc must have the same data type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (scale parameter as a primitive float or integer must be strictly positive)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 6 (probability value p as a primitive float or integer must be strictly between 0 and 1)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 < 1
>>
Rule 7 (tensors p and scale must have valid domains when non-empty)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0) ∨ (min(v_1) > 0 ∧ max(v_1) < 1 ∧ min(v_2) > 0)
>>
Rule 8 (tensors must either have matching dimensions or at least one is a scalar 0D tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0)
